--TEST--
a subscript whose base has already answered that it holds no array is refused where it is written — a scalar, a `string`, an untested `?array<T>`, and a `mixed` in a *write* target — `rule:types/arrays`, `rule:types/string-is-utf8`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/arrays` checks an element read and write against the array's *declared*
// element type, so a base that declares none has nothing to name and nothing
// to check the read against. PHP answers `null` with a warning for most of
// these — `rule:types/a-declared-type-answers-before-the-program-runs`'s family — and Novis refuses at check time instead.
// A `string` is not an exception: `rule:types/string-is-utf8` indexes one by extended
// grapheme cluster through `Core\Str`, deliberately not through a subscript.
// The `?array<string>` is the sharpest: a nullable array has an element type
// only once it is known not to be `null`, so an *untested* one is refused here
// while the same subscript inside an `if ($rows != null)` narrows and runs
// (`nvs_types::locals`' narrowing docs own that half).
//
// `mixed` is the one base that is *not* refused for a read: it is `rule:types/conversion`
// 's unchecked position, so whether there is an array here is the tag's
// question and not the site's, exactly as `rule:types/erased-member-access` defers a property
// access through an erased receiver. Only the **write** below is refused —
// an element write separates a copy-on-write buffer and needs a holder to
// write the separated one back through, which a value that is only a tag does
// not name.
mixed $m = "x";
$m["0"] = "1";
echo $m["0"], "\n";
int $i = 1;
echo $i["0"], "\n";
string $s = "abc";
echo $s["0"], "\n";
?array<string> $rows = null;
echo $rows["0"], "\n";
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0482]: `mixed` cannot be subscripted
   --> case.nvs:21:1
%A
error[E0482]: `int` cannot be subscripted
   --> case.nvs:24:6
%A
error[E0482]: `string` cannot be subscripted
   --> case.nvs:26:6
%A
error[E0482]: `null|array<string>` cannot be subscripted
   --> case.nvs:28:6
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
